WEBVTT

00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:15,130
of Instagram and Facebook videos and posts that claim this or that nutrient

00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:21,630
cures cancer. What do you have to say about these clips? I'd say be very very

00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:27,790
careful. So I'm not afraid of that. I just do not like alternative practitioners.

00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:34,030
They might have the best part, excuse me, in the world and they're trying to help

00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:39,370
cancer patients, you know, immensely. They're trying to give the best advice but

00:00:39,370 --> 00:00:45,810
everybody is unique. And to say, oh, this cures cancer, I've seen Facebook posts

00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:51,430
like that where people make up, make, create really pretty memes that say,

00:00:51,430 --> 00:01:00,210
it tumor kills cancer in 100% or some silly thing like that. Well, the truth is

00:01:00,210 --> 00:01:05,370
if you took a petri dish and you put cancer cells in there, you could put

00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:09,170
evaporated water in with it, it would probably kill the cancer cells. So

00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:13,130
it doesn't mean that evaporated water kills cancer cells or some silly

00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:17,570
things like that. It's just to me, it's just foolishness. Everybody's physiology is

00:01:17,570 --> 00:01:22,250
different. You got to look at the big picture. You got to treat people individually.

00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:28,610
And I think it gives alternative practitioners a black eye, honestly, when you see

00:01:28,610 --> 00:01:35,450
claims like that, or when you see quote-unquote nutritious make certain claims

00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:43,210
that are just not, that are not completely honest. And I think that's, there's

00:01:43,210 --> 00:01:49,010
danger in that. I think it gives people, you know, wrong thoughts about what's

00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:55,570
going to help deal with their cancer or their serious disease. I see a lot of

00:01:55,570 --> 00:01:59,810
Instagram posts like that and it's, I just unfollow those people because it's

00:01:59,810 --> 00:02:04,530
just, I think they influence people the wrong way. Especially we live in this

00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:08,210
world of influencers, right? Are you going to be careful who you are allowing

00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:13,770
to influence you? The Bible is very clear that we're supposed to be careful that we

00:02:13,770 --> 00:02:23,850
protect our mind so that we don't allow bad influencers who all sorts of that

00:02:23,850 --> 00:02:29,250
going on. So you have to be careful with that. So no, I don't say there's not

00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:35,530
validity in anything, but when you start making claims, then you do have to

00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:40,970
be careful. I also have a struggle when you hear claims. And I just talked to

00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:44,090
somebody the other day that they said they're starting to drink alkaline water

00:02:44,090 --> 00:02:49,570
because doctors so and so said that alkaline water is the best thing. Oh my

00:02:49,570 --> 00:02:55,930
word. It's like I've talked about this in the past lots of times. That's just

00:02:55,930 --> 00:03:00,130
not the right thing to do. Please don't do that. You're not alkalizing your

00:03:00,130 --> 00:03:05,570
system when you are drinking alkaline water. You're not alkalizing your system.

00:03:05,570 --> 00:03:12,930
You're not doing anything from an oral standpoint. So it's just, it's just really

00:03:12,930 --> 00:03:24,330
poor understanding of physiology. And that just makes me really sad.

